course: dictionary
lesson: 13041
title: Fantasia: music, mixes and a film
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A fantasia is a piece of music written freely. The composer follows their own imagination instead of a strict pattern, so the music can wander and surprise you. «The pianist began softly, then her fantasia rushed off in all directions.» Here, fantasia means a free, imaginative piece of music.
explain: Fantasia can also mean a mix of tunes. «The brass band ended with a fantasia of famous sea songs» means they played several well-known tunes joined together. Clues like "of" and a list of tunes tell you this meaning.
explain: Fantasia can also be a name. «We watched Fantasia on a rainy Sunday» means the 1940 Disney film, which is set to classical music. A capital F and a film in the sentence are your clues.
explain: Use the context to decide. Ask: is this about a piece of music, a mix of tunes, or a film? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A fantasia is a piece of music written freely, following the composer's imagination rather than a strict pattern.
fact: «Fantasia» can also mean a mixture of well-known tunes played together.
fact: Fantasia is also the name of a 1940 Disney film set to classical music.
fact: Vaughan Williams wrote a famous «Fantasia on Greensleeves», which is a good example of the music meaning.
fact: A quick check: swap in "a free piece of music" or "a mix of tunes" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The pianist's fantasia wandered wherever her imagination led.» What is a fantasia here? | *A piece of music written freely | A map of the sea | A strict, measured dance | A tall, old castle
exercise: «The brass band ended with a fantasia of famous sea songs.» What does fantasia mean here? | *A mix of well-known tunes played together | A single, very quiet note | A list of new words | A cold, windy day at sea
exercise: Mia says, «Let's watch Fantasia tonight.» Fantasia is the name of what? | A dance from Spain | A type of sandwich | A famous football team | *A 1940 Disney film set to classical music
test: «Vaughan Williams wrote a Fantasia on Greensleeves for orchestra.» What does fantasia tell us about this piece? | A mix of new words | Ready-made, with a strict pattern to follow | *Written freely, following the composer's imagination | A famous film about the sea
test: Which sentence uses fantasia as the name of a film? | *«We watched Fantasia on a rainy Sunday.» | «The pianist's fantasia wandered in all directions.» | «The band played a fantasia of sea songs.» | «The fantasia was played very softly at dawn.»
exam: In «The composer's fantasia flowed wherever his imagination led», what does fantasia mean? | A strict pattern that must never change | A film about a rainy Sunday | *A piece of music written freely, following the imagination | A tiny insect that lives in the sea
